+/// \brief A string stream that does not swallow an allocation failure
+///
+/// SaturnExplorer: libstdc++ (and libc++) catch a \b std::bad_alloc thrown while the buffer of an
+/// \b std::ostringstream grows, and only set the stream's badbit, so the text is cut short and
+/// nothing is reported: a warning ("Removing unreac"), a name, a number. The engine builds the text
+/// of its warnings, comments and messages in these. Setting badbit as an exception mask makes the
+/// insertion rethrow the original exception, which the host reports as an out-of-memory failure.
+class ostringstream : public std::ostringstream {
+public:
+  ostringstream(void) { exceptions(std::ios_base::badbit); }
+};
